Fourteenth Challenge/Solution pair. Proves, for every dimension N, g ≥ 0, L,
cap function C, exponent vector e and weight p, that ∫_{T̃} (L − Σx)^p ∏ xᵢ^{eᵢ}
equals the closed form gramGen (integral_supportT_gen), reusing V2b's
stratification, translation and Fubini steps with new counting over the
placements of the distinguished coordinates (sig_insert, sig_union, sig_card).
Adds symmetry, rationality, consistency with V2b, and a transport theorem
(gramGen_extend) to the d-indexed form gramFin; connects to V0's generators
(gram_entry_gen_list) and shows every Table 3 I_T entry on B21 is an explicit
rational (gram_entry_B21_rat). Worked example with two distinguished
coordinates: I_T[(1,(2)),(0,(2))] = ∫ (L − P₁)P₂² (gram_entry_example), value
kernel-checked cell by cell and equal to V2a's moment computation. Comparator
suite gram_general_v2c added (14 suites); controls and result record included.
Axioms: propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
