+      result: "rejected"
+    - change: "integral_supportT_gen claimed with weight p + 1 in the Challenge"
+      result: "rejected: 'Challenge and solution theorem statement do not match: BGP212.Challenge.integral_supportT_gen'"
+  resources:
+    new_mathlib_modules: "none beyond V2b"
+    proof_modules: "Solution.GramGeneral elaborates in under a minute; no kernel arithmetic"
+    certificate_build: "Solution.GramGeneralCert: about 19 minutes (1135 s), peak 4.7 GB; 531 cell lemmas, 89 row lemmas"
+    per_cell_cost: "about 10 s and about 1.5 GB above the import baseline per nonzero cell (row r, placement (A, B)); memory is released between declarations"
+    comparator_suite: "about 21 minutes 40 seconds in the build container (it replays the certificate)"
+    disk: "about 7.4 MB of new build artefacts (GramGeneralCert.olean 2.2 MB); no new Mathlib modules"
+    design_finding: >
+      Evaluated directly, the N-indexed closed form gramGen is out of reach for the kernel (one
+      row exceeded 8 GB): every placement term walks products and piFinset over all 45
+      coordinates. The transport theorem gramGen_extend moves the evaluation to gramFin, with
+      loops over the d distinguished coordinates only; this is a proved reduction, so the
+      certificate's cost scales with d and the number of placements (3^d), not with N.
+    scaling_estimate: >
